Once `PlanarTopology`'s `Surface.eulerChar`, `Surface.IsOrientable`, `Surface.Orientation`,
and `boundaryComponentCount` exist, add the decisive milestones:

  -- Under the first two surface conditions the boundary is the image of the `α₂`-fixed
  -- sides, one circle per component of the boundary 1-map.
  theorem GMap2.boundary_realization (h₀ : ∀ d, G.adj 0 d ≠ d) (h₁ : ∀ d, G.adj 1 d ≠ d) : ...
  theorem GMap2.boundaryComponentCount_realization (h₀) (h₁) :
      boundaryComponentCount G.realization = G.boundaryComponentCount

  -- Under the full surface condition the orbit cells are the cells of the realization.
  theorem IsSurfaceGMap.eulerChar_eq (h : IsSurfaceGMap G) :
